WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.670 --> 00:00:03.137
- Someone has to say action
or else I'm not gonna talk.

00:00:03.137 --> 00:00:04.050
- [Crew Member] Action!

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:07.217
(upbeat music)
- Woo.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:12.190
Welcome back to "Making it Big."

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:15.130
This is the show where I
take food that people love

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:17.100
and I make giant versions of them.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.760
What am I doing, you might ask.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:22.660
Well, today we are gonna
be making a giant Kit Kat.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:25.890
We have some very expensive
Valrhona chocolate.

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:27.390
We've already been
tempering this chocolate

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:30.430
for about 40 minutes with
a method known sous vide.

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:34.410
This is a machine that
keeps water circulating

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:35.680
at a fixed temperature.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:38.180
This helps the chocolate set its structure

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:40.130
so that it stays shiny, stay snappy,

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:41.890
and if we're gonna make giant Kit Kat,

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:43.820
we might as well do this the right way.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:47.900
So I want to keep squishing
these bags of chocolate

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:49.510
and giving them a nice massage

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:52.171
and see you guys when
the chocolate's ready.

00:00:52.171 --> 00:00:53.700
(upbeat music)

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:56.147
Okay, so this chocolate is now tempered.

00:00:56.147 --> 00:00:59.300
I'm drying it off on this towel

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:02.396
because water and
chocolate do not get along.

00:01:02.396 --> 00:01:04.010
They hate each other.

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:07.050
So we have two bags,
there's more in the back.

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:09.070
This is a small fraction

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:11.170
of what we're gonna be using today.

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:12.463
Here we go, ooh-hoo.

00:01:14.817 --> 00:01:17.210
This is like a chocolate waterfall.

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:18.580
You guys see this (beep)?

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:19.720
Oh, can't say that.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:21.310
It's okay, post'll censor it.

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:26.310
So we managed to source large
wafers from a secret store.

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:29.690
Might've been a backroom deal.

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:31.710
My philosophy is if you don't want to know

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:34.490
the answer to the question, you don't ask.

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:38.850
Chocolate is our glue, wafer is our paper.

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:41.530
I was never very good
in arts and craft class,

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:43.280
but I will do my best.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:45.350
Yeah, ooh, ooh, let's go.

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:48.603
We get a smooth layer.

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:52.483
This thing is gonna take a
lot of chocolate, isn't it?

00:01:52.483 --> 00:01:55.140
(upbeat jaunty music)

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:56.870
This is quite satisfying.

00:01:56.870 --> 00:01:59.940
You get to fill in all
these little cracks.

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:04.550
Damn. All right, this is one.

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:08.783
Next one goes on, line it up. Nice.

00:02:09.803 --> 00:02:13.273
Ooh-hoo-hoo. Oh, little chunks.

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:17.650
Wow, it seems like I
have a lot of work to do.

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:19.770
We'll be right back.

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:23.140
Ba-dun-dun-dun-bum-bum.

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:24.490
That's the commercial song.

00:02:26.119 --> 00:02:27.810
After some help with the culinary team,

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:31.040
we have 12 wafers that are all stacked up

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:34.300
with quite a staggering
amount of chocolate.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:37.700
I have one large knife.

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:39.900
I have one ruler.

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:43.343
Whole thing's around 18 inches,
so maybe divide that by six.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:46.010
Pull up the woman with the numbers

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:47.370
doing the meme numbers here.

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:49.718
Straight-ish down with
a little bit of rocking.

00:02:49.718 --> 00:02:52.635
(wafers crunching)

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:56.560
Woo! That's cool.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:58.182
Here we go, steady hand.

00:02:58.182 --> 00:03:01.099
(wafers crunching)

00:03:03.136 --> 00:03:07.650
Woo, one, two, three,
four, five, six bricks.

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:09.270
Oh, you know like in the music videos

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:11.440
when the rappers hold up
like the money to their ear

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:12.770
and they're just like.

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:15.050
I have bands and stacks.

00:03:15.050 --> 00:03:16.940
I have Gs and racks.

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:21.780
Gotta get the money 'cause
I'm fly like a honey.

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:23.683
I'm slangin' them bricks.

00:03:25.355 --> 00:03:28.700
I think that means something else though.

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:31.088
I'm gonna get so much (beep) for this.

00:03:31.088 --> 00:03:32.410
(upbeat music)

00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:36.900
This is a large Pullman loaf
pan used for bread making

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:40.700
that happens to be in the perfect size

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:43.810
for those Kit Kat signature ingots.

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:45.320
You know when you guys open a Kit Kat

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:49.380
and you see the words Kit
Kat on the bar itself?

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:51.020
Well, this is my show.

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:53.400
I'm going to put my name.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:57.670
We have acetate strips, commonly
used in baking or pastry

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:00.100
to deal with cakes and
things of that sorts.

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:03.760
We have honey as an edible glue,

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:05.680
and we have five letters.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:09.230
The tricky part is that I
have to put them on backwards.

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:11.166
If we put them on and wrote Alvin

00:04:11.166 --> 00:04:12.680
and we flipped the Kit Kat over,

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:14.123
it would say nivla.

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:16.950
That's not my name.

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:21.380
Give this a nice little glue,
damn, that's sticky, okay.

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:23.856
A-L-V-I, I.

00:04:23.856 --> 00:04:25.810
If I do this correctly,

00:04:25.810 --> 00:04:28.610
this should spell Alvin to the camera.

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:30.160
Does it spell Alvin?

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:34.370
The pan has now been lined
with our acetate strips,

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:39.370
which means it's time to get
this chocolate into this pan.

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:41.033
I'm going in.

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:45.460
Ooh, that's real nice.

00:04:45.460 --> 00:04:47.100
I really like that.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:50.830
Gotta make sure we get as
much of this out as we can.

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:52.500
This is not cheap.

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:54.020
My mom would yell at me.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:55.493
This is gonna be my snack.

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:57.960
This is my personal bag now.

00:04:57.960 --> 00:04:58.793
I've marked it.

00:04:58.793 --> 00:05:01.220
Gotta make sure there's no air bubbles

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:03.680
so that we get all those nice corners.

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:05.693
Oh, I can save it.

00:05:05.693 --> 00:05:07.820
A little wall almost caved in there.

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:08.713
Don't do that.

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:12.310
There you go, now we're good.

00:05:12.310 --> 00:05:14.340
Don't you dare fall on me now.

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:16.160
Now we can go in with the wafer.

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:18.647
I'm gonna lay you down just like that.

00:05:18.647 --> 00:05:20.780
Gotta get the edges.

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:25.780
Get you down in there
too, little buddy. Yeah.

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:27.570
This has set out for a little bit.

00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:29.230
We're gonna get more chocolate in here.

00:05:29.230 --> 00:05:30.740
Here we go.

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:33.963
Ooh, that's so nice. Damn.

00:05:35.871 --> 00:05:37.810
Mm, this is great.

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:41.790
Pop those air bubbles real
quick, boop, boop, boop.

00:05:41.790 --> 00:05:44.790
Little guys seem to be a little,

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:47.100
they're trying to escape
their chocolate prison,

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:49.583
so I wanna push them down like that.

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:54.103
I wanna hold these wafers
underwater, under chocolate,

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:58.193
until they stop moving and struggling.

00:05:59.590 --> 00:06:01.440
That's dark. I'll see you guys in a bit.

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:03.550
(upbeat music)

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:08.550
So now I got one solid
ingot for the Kit Kat

00:06:08.850 --> 00:06:11.280
and here we have a little contraption

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:14.430
that our culinary team was
nice enough to put together.

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:17.890
It has a foil and acetate set up,

00:06:17.890 --> 00:06:21.800
which is where the Kit Kat is
going to be finally assembled.

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:24.145
So there are six pounds

00:06:24.145 --> 00:06:28.120
of high quality chocolate in this bar.

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:30.583
We're just gonna try to
get this first one out.

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:34.423
Ooh, this is a tight fit in here.

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:43.100
Come out.

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:44.513
Oh, is that it?

00:06:45.473 --> 00:06:46.513
That is not it.

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:49.283
Come on.

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:55.530
Ooh, oh man, that's pretty cool.

00:06:55.530 --> 00:06:56.950
Oh, you know what this is like?

00:06:56.950 --> 00:07:00.170
This is like when you
peel the thing on the TV

00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:02.563
and you just go in there
and you get the, yeah.

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:08.810
And then if your parents
are Asian, like mine,

00:07:08.810 --> 00:07:10.750
they never peel it off for some reason

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:12.820
'cause they think it
protects it, which it does,

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:15.770
but then it just looks ugly.

00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:18.670
All right, and I gotta get
my name off of this thing.

00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:20.193
Give me an A. A.

00:07:23.450 --> 00:07:24.880
Give me an L.

00:07:30.066 --> 00:07:31.383
L!

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:36.010
Not bad if I do say so myself.

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:39.710
As you can see the chocolate
right here is nice and shiny,

00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:42.803
which means it has been tempered properly.

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:45.993
Damn. Pretty cool, huh?

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:48.910
Now I really got them bricks.

00:07:48.910 --> 00:07:50.120
I'm gonna ask for some help

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:52.310
from our wonderful culinary team.

00:07:52.310 --> 00:07:53.870
We're gonna make three of these.

00:07:53.870 --> 00:07:56.450
My doctor's not gonna
be very happy with me,

00:07:56.450 --> 00:08:01.401
but hey, this isn't making
it healthy, all right, so.

00:08:01.401 --> 00:08:03.650
(playful music)

00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:07.600
Now the idea is to get them all together

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:12.163
to be one whole Kit Kat, and
we're gonna use more chocolate.

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:15.940
Yeah, buddy.

00:08:15.940 --> 00:08:20.210
All right, spread this
out a bit, ooh-hoo-hoo.

00:08:20.210 --> 00:08:21.950
We've got a good base going.

00:08:21.950 --> 00:08:25.004
This is gonna be one thick Kit Kat.

00:08:25.004 --> 00:08:26.763
Yeah, get that stuff out.

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:30.980
Now we gotta get every single
one of these blocks in.

00:08:30.980 --> 00:08:32.553
Ain't no way to do it,

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:35.353
but just to do it.

00:08:36.312 --> 00:08:37.145
Ooh.

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:45.700
Brick, yeah. One. (chuckles)

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:46.943
Brick number two.

00:08:48.270 --> 00:08:49.980
Ah, yes.

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:51.820
Looks like I gotta make some room.

00:08:51.820 --> 00:08:52.960
I'll make it work.

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:55.240
I've done five seasons of this show.

00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:57.450
Yeah, there we go.

00:08:57.450 --> 00:09:00.063
It's gonna be one thick
ass Kit Kat I'm gonna say.

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:05.160
It has been about one hour.

00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:08.660
This Kit Kat has been
setting in the fridge.

00:09:08.660 --> 00:09:11.700
Fingers crossed 'cause
it's time to take it out.

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:12.943
Gonna take our walls.

00:09:14.465 --> 00:09:18.675
♪ Gimme a piece of that big Kit Kat bar. ♪

00:09:18.675 --> 00:09:21.437
So there's foil underneath the Kit Kat?

00:09:21.437 --> 00:09:22.270
Let's see.

00:09:26.173 --> 00:09:27.370
(tray clatters)

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:29.473
Nice. Physics.

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:33.283
Oops. Last piece.

00:09:34.149 --> 00:09:36.249
We gotta do a little bit in this trimming,

00:09:37.774 --> 00:09:41.032
(playful music)

00:09:41.032 --> 00:09:42.782
also called snacking.

00:09:44.372 --> 00:09:48.640
Approximately 70 years later,
this is a giant Kit Kat.

00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:52.050
This weighs 30 pounds,
six pounds each bar.

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:55.060
And the base itself, also
six pounds of chocolate.

00:09:55.060 --> 00:09:59.100
A culmination of many talented
individuals, culinary team,

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:00.260
making all these bars,

00:10:00.260 --> 00:10:02.440
art team making this beautiful decoration,

00:10:02.440 --> 00:10:06.420
camera and production team
making this look good on camera,

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:09.890
and me, I just ate chocolate all day.

00:10:09.890 --> 00:10:11.753
Let's cut this thing and see what we got.

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:13.763
Come on.

00:10:17.444 --> 00:10:18.277
Whoa.

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:20.283
Look at that.

00:10:20.283 --> 00:10:22.660
Look at that cross section.

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:26.400
And for reference, this
is a normal Kit Kat.

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:29.830
This is what happens when
you give a guy like me

00:10:29.830 --> 00:10:32.820
a lot of creative freedom and money.

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:33.663
Give me a break.

00:10:36.550 --> 00:10:38.423
Woo! Cheers.

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:43.330
Oh, ours tastes good.

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:46.515
Ours taste quite different.

00:10:46.515 --> 00:10:50.103
I do prefer ours because
well, one, we made it.

00:10:51.240 --> 00:10:53.633
And two, it cost a lot more money.

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:57.120
I have a lot of enjoying to do,

00:10:57.120 --> 00:11:00.910
so that being said, see you
guys in the next episode

00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:03.503
where we're gonna continue to make it big.

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:07.560
This is really good.

00:11:08.871 --> 00:11:11.538
(upbeat music)

